OSS wrote:
>
> I've been playing Nethack for about a year, but I'm ...a complete
> newbie at the moment. In most  of my games I clean out the mines and
> comlete the Sokoban, and then I get killed in a way most cruel ;)

That's good progress for only a year.  Each time you die learn
some lesson from it.  Early on the lessons are about what you
were doing at the time of death.  Later the lessons are about a
decision you made a level ago or so.

> I wanted to ask you a couple of questions, the first of them being:
> 1. How do you heal yourself? I mean, you can just rest (space+numpad5),
> but that's time-consuming, ineffective and dangerous. You can also use
> a potion, but there's never enough of them. So, how a Real Nethack
> Player ;) should do it?

Resting is the main way.  Retreat to a shallower level that has
already been cleared out and/or that has weaker monsters.
Wander a bit and return.

There are also potions of healing, extra healing and full healing
as well as spells of healing and extra healing.  They give
different numbers of hit points but they also have additional
beneficial effects.  The spells are particularly usefull for zapping
at pets that are in combat.

> 2. How do you kill cockatrices? Their "touch" effect almost always
> petrifies my characters, even though they(characters) wear full sets of
> armor, etc. How do I kill them? Genocide, maybe?

Read more about missile combat.  Thrown daggers, darts, rocks,
shot arrows.  Wands and spells.  Ranged combat becomes more
and more important as you get deeper - There are monsters that
are far more damaging than cockatrices later on.

If you're having problems picking up the corpses there are three
lessons to be learned.  1) You don't have a full set of armor yet
because you still don't have gloves.  2) You have not yet learned
how to turn off autopickup or to limit it to specific item classes.
3) Type of armor matters far more than you think - AC number
is not the most important feature of armor just the easiest to
see.



